Thought Process
Below is a complete, working solution you can build in the 3-hour window. I chose Python + FastAPI for speed of development and easy testing — the same architecture ports directly to Go or TypeScript if you prefer.

The two design decisions worth calling out (they're what graders will notice):

Status is derived on read, not stored. There's no background thread flipping devices to OFFLINE — every endpoint computes ONLINE/OFFLINE from now - last_heartbeat. No drift, no races, trivially testable.
The clock is injectable. The store takes a clock callable; tests inject a fake clock and verify the exact 30-second boundary deterministically — no sleep(31) in the test suite.
