The 3 things to understand here (interview gold):

_status() (near the bottom) is the 30-second rule. It compares "now" against last_seen_at. If the gap is ≤ 30s → ONLINE, otherwise OFFLINE. It's calculated fresh every time someone asks — no background thread ever flips a device to OFFLINE.
The clock is injectable. By default it's the real clock (utc_now), but tests will pass a fake one they can fast-forward. That's how we'll test "exactly 30 seconds" without waiting 30 real seconds.
self._lock — multiple web requests can hit the store at the same instant; the lock makes sure two heartbeats can't corrupt the same device record.
